State keys are the pipeline's own keys. __none__ stands for a record with no pipeline instance: name it in _in to include such records, or in _nin to leave them out.

Ask for $workflow_instance in fields on any collection bound to a pipeline and each record carries its current instance: the current state (with the name partners are sent, external_label), when it entered that state, and the transitions the caller's role may run from it. Add $workflow_instance.history for the transition log. It is never part of *, a record with no pipeline reads null, and a whole page is read in a fixed number of queries. $state is the lighter read when only the state is needed.
// Current state + available transitions
?fields=id,workflow_id,$workflow_instance

// ... plus the transition log
?fields=id,$workflow_instance.history

// On a related record
?fields=id,workflow.$workflow_instance
Available transitions are filtered by role, not by their condition rules — the transition endpoint still judges those, so a listed transition can be refused.

Every write is recorded with its origin: person, machine, import or integration. $origin filters records by the writes they have received. _in keeps records that have a write of those origins; _nin keeps records that have none. days, since, until, by (an account id) and action (create, update, delete) narrow which writes count.
// Touched by an integration or an import in the last 7 days
?filter={"$origin":{"_in":["integration","import"],"days":7}}

// Never edited by a person
?filter={"$origin":{"_nin":["person"]}}

// Updated by one account since a date
?filter=…
Writes made before origins were stored carry none and match no origin. An origin name that does not exist matches nothing.

A calculated field made of arithmetic or coalesce over the record's own columns can be filtered and sorted like a column; the comparison runs in the database. GET /api/collections/<collection> marks such fields with sql_filterable: true. Any other calculated field, and every rollup that is not stored, exists only after the rows are read: naming one in a filter or sort is refused with 400 FIELD_NOT_FILTERABLE.
// remaining = budget - spent  (a calculated field)
?filter={"remaining":{"_lt":0}}&sort=-remaining

// Any calculated field may be named in fields=, filterable or not
?fields=id,name,remaining,open_order_total

// AND — all conditions must match
?filter={"_and":[{"status":{"_eq":"active"}},{"amount":{"_gt":1000}}]}

// OR — at least one condition matches
?filter={"_or":[{"status":{"_eq":"active"}},{"status":{"_eq":"pending"}}]}

// Nested AND/OR
