Every registered collection is exposed in GraphQL, including hidden ones — hidden is a UI flag (keep it out of the nav), not an API exclusion. Junction collections therefore have full query/mutation fields (e.g. delete_workflows_files_items), matching the REST items API.

The sort argument accepts an array of field paths. Prefix with - for descending. Dotted paths traverse M2O relations via LEFT JOIN.
# Simple multi-field sort
query {
  inventory_requests(sort: ["-submitted_at", "title"]) {
    id title submitted_at
  }
}

# Sort by related field (M2O)
query {
  inventory_requests(sort: ["project.name", "-submitted_at"]) {
    id title
