• Meta keys: reads (collections), record ({collection, id}), fields (only writes naming one of them count; creates, deletes and writes naming no fields always do), aspects ($state, $comments… — aspect notices are ignored otherwise), includeOwn (default on for reads, off for record, whose save already refreshed it), minGapMs (default 10 s for reads, 0 for record; a trailing refresh is never dropped), reconcileOnly. • The bridge joins the collection rooms that active tagged queries read and leaves them 30 s after the last one goes. Events coalesce for 300 ms per collection. Only queries on screen refetch; the rest are marked stale and refetch when they next mount. A hidden tab marks stale and refetches when it is shown again. • Reconcile — every tagged query plus the active record, list, queue, My Work and widget reads refetch once — after a reconnect whose catch-up could not replay the gap (status().resumed is unverified), on nvr:catchup-full, and when a tab comes back after being hidden five minutes or more. A reconnect that replayed every missed event does not reconcile. • At sign-in the server sends catchup:cursor {seq} — the event journal position — so a tab that has not received an event yet still replays its gap after a reconnect instead of missing it. • Permissions: the refetch runs through the query’s own route as the viewer. An event naming a record the viewer cannot read only re-asks for what they could already see. • The notification badge, the Issue log, broadcast receipts, a record’s partner submissions, a help video’s render status and the chat Online list follow socket events the same way: while the socket is live their polls drop to a safety net (five minutes; two for the badge, since a timed snooze coming back sends no event). Operations pages with no event behind them (Traffic Map, health, logs, jobs, crons) keep polling, and only while the tab is visible.

